---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="License — Limitcode Pro"
  description="Limitcode Pro licensing terms: individual and business licenses, perpetual access, offline grace period, and ownership."
  canonicalPath="/license/"
>

  <Nav />

  <main class="license-page">
    <section class="container license-wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Licensing Terms</span>
      <h1>Limitcode Pro License</h1>

      <p class="license-intro">
        Limitcode Pro is a native AI coding agent plugin built for Sublime Text 4.
        Limitcode Pro is proprietary software, copyrighted by Jawuil (Jawuil Labs).
        The separate open-source edition of Limitcode is governed by its own open-source
        license in its respective GitHub repository.
      </p>

      <h2>Summary (TL;DR)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>One-time purchase, perpetual fallback:</strong> Your license grants permanent
          use of Limitcode Pro and includes <strong>1 full year of free updates</strong>. After one
          year, the last version released within your update window continues working indefinitely
          with no recurring subscription required.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Individual vs. Business use:</strong> Both individual and organization licenses are
          valid for commercial work. Individual licenses are tied to a single person (up to 3 machines
          used by that person). Organization-purchased licenses are licensed per seat (1 license per
          developer, up to 3 machines per seat) and can be reassigned within the company.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Offline grace period:</strong> License activation requires a periodic online check,
          with up to <strong>30 days of offline grace</strong> between checks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero data middleman:</strong> Prompts, files, and API keys go directly from your
          machine to your chosen AI provider or local model. Limitcode servers never store or proxy
          your source code.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>1. Individual Licenses</h2>
      <p>If you are an individual purchasing a license with your own personal funds:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You are granted a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use Limitcode Pro
          on up to <strong>three (3) computers</strong> (Windows, macOS, or Linux) that you personally use.
        </li>
        <li>
          You may use an Individual License for both personal projects and commercial/work software
          development, provided you are the sole user of the software on those machines.
        </li>
        <li>Individual licenses may not be shared with other people or transferred to another person.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>2. Business &amp; Organization Licenses</h2>
      <p>If a company, team, or legal entity purchases licenses with organization funds:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Licenses are granted on a <strong>per-seat (per-user)</strong> basis. Each individual developer
          using Limitcode Pro requires one (1) license seat.
        </li>
        <li>
          Sharing a single license's 3-device activation limit across multiple employees is strictly
          prohibited. Each licensed seat allows the assigned employee to activate Limitcode Pro on up to
          three (3) computers used by that employee.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transferability:</strong> Unlike Individual Licenses, Business Licenses owned by an
          organization may be reassigned to a different team member if the original assignee leaves the
          company or stops using the software.
        </li>
        <li>For multi-seat keys or custom company invoices, contact <code>hola@jawuil.dev</code>.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>3. Updates &amp; Perpetual Access</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Every license includes <strong>one (1) full year of software updates</strong> starting from the
          date of purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          Once the 1-year update window expires, you retain the perpetual right to continue using any
          version of Limitcode Pro released prior to your expiration date on your eligible devices.
          Renewing for future updates is entirely optional.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>4. General Restrictions &amp; Ownership</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Copyright (c) 2026 Jawuil (limitcode.jawuil.dev). All rights reserved.</strong></li>
        <li>Limitcode Pro may not be sub-licensed, resold, published, or redistributed.</li>
        <li>
          You may not publicly share your license key, bypass or tamper with the license verification
          mechanism, or decompile, reverse-engineer, or create derivative works of the proprietary
          package without prior written consent from the author.
        </li>
        <li>
          No title or intellectual property rights in Limitcode Pro are transferred to the licensee.
          You retain 100% ownership and responsibility for any code, patches, or outputs generated in
          your projects.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>5. Disclaimer of Warranty &amp; Liability</h2>
      <p class="disclaimer">
        THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
        BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
        NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
        DAMAGES (INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, LOSS OF DATA, SOURCE CODE MODIFICATIONS, SHELL COMMAND
        EXECUTION, OR THIRD-PARTY API CHARGES) OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT,
        TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
        DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .license-page {
    padding: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px) 0 clamp(64px, 8vw, 120px);
  }

  .license-wrap {
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .license-wrap .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--signal);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .license-wrap .eyebrow .dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--signal);
  }

  .license-wrap h1 {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .license-wrap h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.2vw, 1.95rem);
    margin: 30px 0 14px;
  }

  .license-wrap p,
  .license-wrap li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .license-intro {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }

  .license-wrap p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .license-wrap ul {
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .license-wrap li {
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .license-wrap code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
  }

  .license-wrap hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin: 28px 0;
  }

  .disclaimer {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
</style>
